          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life of Leonardo da Vinci</strong><br>\nLeonardo da Vinci was born on April 15, 1452, in Vinci, Italy. As a child, he showed a keen interest in nature and mechanics, which would influence his diverse studies later in life. Leonardo received an informal education in Latin, geometry, and mathematics but was mostly self-taught in scientific observation.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Apprenticeship with Verrocchio</strong><br>\nAt the age of 14, Leonardo began an apprenticeship with the artist Andrea del Verrocchio in Florence. Here, he honed his skills in painting and sculpture. Leonardo's talent was so apparent that, according to some accounts, Verrocchio decided never to paint again after seeing Leonardo's work.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Painting and Sculpture</strong><br>\nLeonardo's painting \"The Last Supper\" and his drawing \"The Vitruvian Man\" are widely celebrated for their composition and understanding of human anatomy. His work on sculptures, though fewer in number, showcased a grasp of the body's structure and movement that was ahead of his time.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
