          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Architectural and Engineering Work</strong><br>\nLeonardo also took on architectural and engineering projects, devising plans for fortifications and public buildings. He was also consulted for his engineering expertise on projects like the diversion of rivers, which demonstrated his practical skills.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Influence and Legacy</strong><br>\nLeonardo's work influenced countless artists and inventors, establishing a legacy that extends far beyond the Renaissance era. His multidisciplinary approach to science and art marked the transition to new ways of thinking and learning during the Renaissance.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Final Years and Death</strong><br>\nLeonardo spent his last years in France, under the patronage of King Francis I. He continued to work on his scientific studies until his death on May 2, 1519, in Amboise, France. Leonardo is remembered as a true polymath and genius of the Renaissance.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
